        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>Given the sets $A = \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$ and $B = \\{3, 4, 5, 6\\}$, find $A \\cap B$ and $A \\cup B$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The intersection $A \\cap B$ consists of elements common to both $A$ and $B$, which are $3$ and $4$. Thus, $A \\cap B = \\{3, 4\\}$.<br>The union $A \\cup B$ consists of all elements in $A$ or $B$ or both, which are $1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6$. Thus, $A \\cup B = \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\}$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
